{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509580-will-we-get-a-m20-otherworlds-sourcebook","id":1509580,"title":"Will we get a M20 otherworlds' sourcebook?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-25T07:10:44-07:00","id":1509580,"title":"Will we get a M20 otherworlds' sourcebook?","content":"Or update for Book of Worlds/The Infinite Tapestry?<br /> <br /> Although M20 core has said both of them are quite out of date, but tbh they're still the best (and only!) otherworlds' books in MtA, and maybe the best in the whole WoD, for those of other lines are simply too focused on their own worlds (WtA Umbra for 13 Realms, for example)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T08:21:26-07:00","id":1509585,"title":"","content":"No further books for Mage have been approved at this time (or the other 20th lines for that matter).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T08:27:43-07:00","id":1509721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509580-will-we-get-a-m20-otherworlds-sourcebook?p=1509585#post1509585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No further books for Mage have been approved at this time (or the other 20th lines for that matter).</div> </div> </div> </div>When you reveal dark tidings, even if it's common knowledge, please cushion them somehow. Offer some tea, a seat, ask how we've been, if we need something, then go <i>We have to talk</i>. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12911-lateral-psychotropy","name":"Lateral.Psychotropy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T08:35:22-07:00","id":1509724,"title":"","content":"Eh. Onyx Path's World of Darkness supplements have been on borrowed time for as far back as the release of Technocracy Reloaded; every book that's come out since then has been a blessing. <br /> <br /> And I'm not willing to throw in the towel; \u201cnothing new has been approved\u201d means simply that. It doesn't mean that the M20 line is done; until such time as M5 gets announced, or Onyx Path <i>says </i>that M20 is done, it's not done. And even then, there's Storyteller's Vault.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T12:20:04-07:00","id":1509759,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking about a sort of &quot;Guide to the Otherworlds&quot; for quite some time. <i>Beyond the Barriers: The Book of Worlds</i> was the first Mage supplement I ever got. It's probably my favorite supplement to any WOD game. The fact that it is probably the largest supplement non-hardcover works for it too. I've been toying around with various updates to the WOD cosmology for awhile now, as evidenced by many of my posts on these forums. I've also come up with not just a possible outline for the book, but an idea for a supplement focusing just on spirits as a go-along &quot;stretch goal&quot; kind of thing so that there would be more room in the main book. Don't get me wrong, <i>Infinite Tapestry</i> wasn't bad, but it focused mostly on the High Umbra, leaving most of the rest as 'see individual game-lines,' and a bit on the Deep Umbra. At the very least, I feel that this could be of great interest, as Mages can and do go everywhere they can in the Umbra, while most of the other splats tend to stick to the ones they know best. A few things got added, such as KOTE's Yomi World and Demon's 'pocket dimensions' that needed Mage treatment. If I could just find the time, interest, and/or assistance, I almost would do it myself. The main sticking point is that I lost the majority of my WOD to flooding about twenty years ago, and I was never able to get much of it back. I only got back into it a few years ago, and I've mostly been sticking to the 20th anniversary material and 5th since then. I just don't have access to the dozens of books to reference, as well as the resources (i.e. finances, computer memory) to get many of the older ones or the SV materials that could be of interest. Maybe one day. Until then, I just have my head cannon theories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T22:55:19-07:00","id":1509838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509580-will-we-get-a-m20-otherworlds-sourcebook?p=1509759#post1509759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been thinking about a sort of &quot;Guide to the Otherworlds&quot; for quite some time. <i>Beyond the Barriers: The Book of Worlds</i> was the first Mage supplement I ever got. It's probably my favorite supplement to any WOD game. The fact that it is probably the largest supplement non-hardcover works for it too. I've been toying around with various updates to the WOD cosmology for awhile now, as evidenced by many of my posts on these forums.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too. Although M20 says it's &quot;quite out of date&quot;, the fact is they made no update during M20. Tbh I really want to translate it into my own language, it seems like I can't wait a M20 version or simply WoD one which contains all lines' cosmologies<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509580-will-we-get-a-m20-otherworlds-sourcebook?p=1509759#post1509759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main sticking point is that I lost the majority of my WOD to flooding about twenty years ago, and I was never able to get much of it back. I only got back into it a few years ago, and I've mostly been sticking to the 20th anniversary material and 5th since then. I just don't have access to the dozens of books to reference, as well as the resources (i.e. finances, computer memory) to get many of the older ones or the SV materials that could be of interest. Maybe one day. Until then, I just have my head cannon theories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good luck!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T11:10:47-07:00","id":1511631,"title":"","content":"By my current thoughts, there is just too much to contain in one book. <i>Beyond the Barriers: The Book of Worlds</i> was one of the larger supplements in WOD history, and it still didn't cover everything. Wraith and Changeling were still fairly new, so the details on the Underworld and the Dreaming were still being clarified. Also, areas covered in detail in other supplements (namely <i>The Book of Chantries, Digital Web, </i>and <i>Horizon: Stronghold of Hope</i>) were also left out. This would have added at least another thirty some pages if covered. Other supplements added newer rules (see <i>Spirit Ways</i>). Since then, other game lines have added even more areas (Kindred of the East Yomi hells, Mummy relocated deathlands/respawning area, Demon pocket dimensions). This could add well over a dozen pages to just give basic information. Currently, I'm thinking at least three volumes would do everything justice.<br /> Volume One would give a general overview of the Otherworlds in the first chapter, with each of the next four chapters covering each of the &quot;big four&quot; areas: Astral/High Umbra, Spirit Wilds/Velvet Shadow/Middle Umbra, Underworld/Low Umbra, the Dreaming + material for the Maya/Dreamzone as the two are generally confused. Chapter six would be a catch-all for the enigmas, anything that didn't fit elsewhere; Chapter Seven would be a listing of all Horizon Realms with a few other similar artificially-created realms like Paradox Realms; and Chapter Eight would be the Deep Umbra and anything else found out there. Appendices would just give extra rules for dealing with the Umbra.<br /> Volume Two would be the 'Book of Sprits.' The first chapter would be an overview of spirits and how to treat and deal with them. Again, each of the next four chapters would give examples of the spirit types found there, with a wider selection than what was included in <i>Gods and Monsters</i>, in the same order. Chapter six will again deal with anything else found in the realms, while chapter seven goes over Deep Umbra horror types. Chapter eight would deal with Bygones and how tell the difference between them and regular spirits. The appendix would be rules for spirit and bygone creation.<br /> The final volume would be sort of a combined player's guide/storyteller handbook for Otherworlds. The first chapter would contain detailed character creation rules: secondary abilities, specialty Backgrounds, spirit-based Merit and Flaws, Rotes, and Wonders. Chapter two would deal with crossing-over with other splats, how they get into the Otherworlds and how they survive there. Chapter three would deal with the mysteries of the Digital Web, from the Tradition's viewpoint, and how it interacts with everywhere else. Chapter four would introduce totally new areas one can add to their own Umbral adventures, with examples from each part of the Umbra. Chapter five would be storyteller advice on playing in the Umbra, as well as creating new spirits/rules/realms/cosmologies to suit their own needs. Anything else would be determined later.<br /> I even have the inklings for a fourth book creating a new type of Umbrood/Bygone splat, but I don't want to spoil such a thing just yet, although I have had the idea since <i>Bygone Bestiary</i> came out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":17984,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","user":"Toby Weingarten","date":".  Needed to paragraph for easier reading. 05-21-2023, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T10:44:19-07:00","id":1511884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509580-will-we-get-a-m20-otherworlds-sourcebook?p=1509724#post1509724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. Onyx Path's World of Darkness supplements have been on borrowed time for as far back as the release of Technocracy Reloaded; every book that's come out since then has been a blessing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is fortunate and good that <i>Technocracy Reloaded</i> was finally released, despite the delays and the relatively small amount of M20 books and supplements. I have started reading this supplement recently, and I have to say that the writings and paragraphs in the book are definitely a nice and welcome sign and indication.<br /> <br /> There is definite progression in regard to the portrayal of Enlightened Scientists of the various Conventions. ( Syndicate, NWO, Progenitors, Void Enginners, ITeration-X - to mention all of them ) I have also noticed distinct advancement in regard to general growth, stability, design, and development of Mage: the Ascension and the World of Darkness as a setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T12:40:49-07:00","id":1511900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lateral.Psychotropy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509580-will-we-get-a-m20-otherworlds-sourcebook?p=1509721#post1509721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When you reveal dark tidings, even if it's common knowledge, please cushion them somehow. Offer some tea, a seat, ask how we've been, if we need something, then go <i>We have to talk</i>. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely, just to look at what they've done in V5 (I'm holding myself with all my strength to not use nasty words lol) and think that The 20th editions won't be continued makes me sink in a deep depression lol, the only relief is to think that I don't need more books to keep my chronicles going, but even so, it's better to not think about this question. I'm so concerned and really afraid of what they'll do with M5 that I have to force myself to <b>not </b>think about it.On the other hand, I still have a likely &quot;futile&quot; hope that they're still going to release more books for M20 and the other lines. I must have hope after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}